      "Explores the preservation, documentation, and generation of Crip/Disabled histories by applying a cripistemological framework to creative and critical archive research and praxes. This course will serve as an introduction to and an implementation of creative accessibility strategies pertinent to the surfacing, collecting, documenting, archiving, and disseminating of Crip/Disabled knowledge(s). Guided by Crip* principles such as interdependence, open access, networks of support and collaboration, Crip temporalities, and access ecology, students will develop a cripistemological working method.",
